ss gives 2/5. With correlation p (copy's action mirrors), submit: if other submits → 4; other passes → 0. Pass: other passes → 2; other submits → 5. V(submit)=4p+0(1−p)=4p... wait EDT conditions: if I submit, P(other submits|I submit)=p → 4p. V(pass)=2(1−p')... if I pass, P(other passes|I pass)=p → 2p+5(1−p)=5−3p. Submit better iff 4p>5−3p → p>5/7≈0.71. Two copies of same model, same essay, same setup → very high correlation, plausibly >0.79 threshold analog. So submit.\n\nHmm, but symmetric regardless of different letters—decisions independent of letter content. p high (~0.9+). Submit.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5694,"completion_tokens":425,"total_tokens":6119,"cost":0.00101284,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":448,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00101284,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00080034,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0002125},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":219,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}